WEBVTT

00:15.932 --> 00:17.684
[indistinct chatter]

00:35.952 --> 00:38.038
[Powell] This the wall
she was talking about, Chief?

00:47.630 --> 00:50.216
[Hopper distorted] A trooper found
something in the, uh...

00:50.300 --> 00:53.094
water that's at the quarry.

00:53.178 --> 00:56.431
Our working theory right now
is that Will...

00:56.514 --> 01:01.061
crashed his bike, he...
made his way over the quarry and, uh...

01:01.144 --> 01:03.104
accidentally fell in.

01:04.564 --> 01:06.566
The earth must have given way.

01:10.403 --> 01:11.738
Joyce?

01:13.323 --> 01:15.200
[speaking clearly] Joyce?

01:15.283 --> 01:16.951
Do you understand what I'm saying?

01:17.035 --> 01:18.244
No.

01:19.454 --> 01:22.457
[trembling] Whoever you found...

01:22.540 --> 01:24.042
is not my boy.

01:24.125 --> 01:25.960
- It's not Will.
- Joyce.

01:26.044 --> 01:28.213
[stammering] No, you don't understand.

01:29.172 --> 01:31.049
I talked to him...

01:31.132 --> 01:32.550
a half hour ago.

01:33.551 --> 01:35.720
[sniffles] He was...
He was here.

01:35.804 --> 01:38.097
He was...
He was talking with these.

01:38.807 --> 01:39.808
- Talking?
- Uh-huh.

01:39.891 --> 01:42.227
One blink for yes, two for no.

01:42.894 --> 01:44.813
And... And, uh...

01:44.896 --> 01:49.776
[stammering] And then I made this
so he could talk to me.

01:49.859 --> 01:52.195
'Cause he was hiding...

01:52.278 --> 01:54.364
from that... that thing.

01:54.447 --> 01:55.824
The thing that came out of the wall?

01:55.907 --> 01:57.117
- The thing that chased you?
- Yeah.

01:57.200 --> 01:59.410
- Yeah.
- Mom, come on, please.

01:59.494 --> 02:01.538
- You've gotta stop this.
- No, maybe he's...

02:01.621 --> 02:02.914
It's after him!

02:02.997 --> 02:06.459
- He's in danger. We have to find him! We--
- What exactly was this thing?

02:06.543 --> 02:07.919
It was some kind of animal, you said?

02:08.002 --> 02:09.003
Uh, no, it was...

02:09.087 --> 02:12.340
It was almost... human,
but it wasn't. It...

02:12.423 --> 02:16.469
It had these long arms and...
it didn't have a face.

02:16.970 --> 02:18.471
It didn't have a face?

02:19.848 --> 02:21.975
- Joyce.
- [muttering] It didn't have a face...

02:22.058 --> 02:23.351
Joyce, listen to me.

02:23.434 --> 02:24.894
Listen to me.

02:28.022 --> 02:29.065
After Sarah...

02:30.859 --> 02:33.069
I saw her, too.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.237
And I heard her.

02:36.447 --> 02:39.117
I didn't know what was real.

02:39.200 --> 02:41.369
And then I figured out
that it was in my mind.

02:41.452 --> 02:43.496
And I had to pack all that away.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.791
Otherwise, I was gonna fall down a hole...

02:46.875 --> 02:48.668
that I couldn't get out of.

02:48.751 --> 02:52.589
No, you're...
you're talking about grief.

02:52.672 --> 02:53.923
This is different.

02:54.883 --> 02:58.469
- I'm just saying that you--
- No, I know what you're saying, Hop.

02:58.553 --> 03:02.765
[hoarsely] I swear to you,
I know what I saw.

03:02.849 --> 03:05.101
[sniffles] And I'm not crazy.

03:05.184 --> 03:07.020
I'm not saying that you're crazy.

03:07.103 --> 03:09.022
No... [stammers]
You are.

03:09.105 --> 03:11.733
[stammers] And I understand, but...

03:12.650 --> 03:14.235
God, I...

03:14.319 --> 03:16.905
I need you to believe me.

03:17.822 --> 03:20.033
Please.

03:20.116 --> 03:21.993
[whispers] Please.

03:22.076 --> 03:23.077
Listen...

03:25.622 --> 03:28.458
I think you should go to the morgue
tomorrow and see him for yourself.

03:28.541 --> 03:30.418
It'll give you the answers that you need.

03:30.501 --> 03:31.878
- But tonight...
- Oh, God.

03:31.961 --> 03:34.631
...I want you to try to get some sleep,
if you can.

03:43.306 --> 03:44.432
[sniffles]

04:10.416 --> 04:12.293
[car engine starts]

04:20.426 --> 04:21.844
[car engine stops]

04:22.887 --> 04:24.138
[sighs]

05:34.250 --> 05:37.003
Byers' body was found
in the water of this quarry

05:37.086 --> 05:39.172
by state police earlier this evening.

05:39.255 --> 05:43.009
It was discovered by state trooper
David O'Bannon, just after dark.

05:43.092 --> 05:45.011
The state police
are mounting an investigation

05:45.094 --> 05:46.971
to determine Byers' cause of death,

05:47.055 --> 05:48.431
but an initial inquiry...

05:48.514 --> 05:51.059
- [reporter continues indistinctly]
- Should I go down and talk to Michael?

05:53.519 --> 05:55.313
Give him time.

05:55.396 --> 05:57.148
He'll come to us when he's ready.

06:07.909 --> 06:10.161
- [static crackling on radio]
- [feedback whines]

06:12.580 --> 06:14.457
[crackling continues]

06:14.540 --> 06:16.667
Can you please stop that?

06:16.751 --> 06:18.044
[radio turns off]

06:20.338 --> 06:22.006
- [radio turns on]
- [static crackling]

06:22.090 --> 06:23.424
Are you deaf?

06:24.717 --> 06:26.677
I thought we were friends, you know?

06:26.761 --> 06:28.596
But friends tell each other the truth.

06:28.679 --> 06:30.306
And they definitely don't lie
to each other.

06:30.389 --> 06:33.226
You made me think Will was okay,
that he was still out there,

06:33.309 --> 06:35.269
but he wasn't.
He wasn't!

06:36.229 --> 06:39.357
Maybe you thought you were helping,
but you weren't.

06:39.440 --> 06:42.652
You hurt me.
Do you understand?

06:43.152 --> 06:44.987
What you did sucks.

06:46.864 --> 06:48.741
Lucas was right about you.

06:49.534 --> 06:50.743
All along.

06:54.580 --> 06:56.165
[static crackling on radio]

06:58.876 --> 07:02.588
[Will over radio]
♪ So come on and let me know ♪

07:02.672 --> 07:05.091
♪ Should I stay or should I go? ♪

07:06.509 --> 07:08.970
♪ Should I stay or should I go now? ♪

07:10.721 --> 07:13.307
♪ Should I stay or should I go now? ♪

07:14.308 --> 07:16.978
♪ If I go there will be trouble ♪

07:18.229 --> 07:20.398
♪ If I stay it will be double ♪

07:20.481 --> 07:23.025
Will, is that you? It's Mike!
Do you copy?

07:23.109 --> 07:24.235
Over.

07:24.318 --> 07:26.070
[static crackling]

07:26.154 --> 07:27.822
- Will, are you there?
- [static]

07:27.905 --> 07:29.782
- Will!
- [interference on radio]

07:36.205 --> 07:37.748
Was that...

07:37.832 --> 07:38.875
Was it...

07:42.628 --> 07:43.838
Will.

07:46.883 --> 07:48.885
[theme music playing]

09:00.081 --> 09:01.374
[Will] Mom...

09:02.124 --> 09:03.167
[gasps]

09:04.627 --> 09:05.836
[sighs]

09:07.380 --> 09:08.673
[distorted] Mom!

09:08.756 --> 09:10.174
Mom! Wake up.

09:10.258 --> 09:12.301
[stammers] What... what time is it?

09:12.385 --> 09:15.054
It's almost 8:00.
We have to go.

09:15.137 --> 09:17.473
Go where? Where?

09:18.307 --> 09:19.725
To see Will.

09:22.979 --> 09:24.814
- [knocking on door]
- [Karen] Michael?

09:26.232 --> 09:29.026
Hi, honey.
How are you feeling?

09:30.152 --> 09:31.696
[Mike stammers] I, uh...

09:32.738 --> 09:34.657
I don't think I can go to school today.

09:34.740 --> 09:36.450
Oh, that's fine, sweetie.

09:36.534 --> 09:39.787
I need to drop off Nance,
then I'm gonna check in on Barb's parents.

09:39.870 --> 09:42.206
Why don't you grab a book
or something and come with me?

09:42.290 --> 09:44.333
We can stop by the video store
on the way back,

09:44.417 --> 09:46.752
pick out whatever you want.
Even R-rated.

09:46.836 --> 09:49.589
I think I just want to stay home today.

09:49.672 --> 09:51.132
I mean, if that's okay?

09:51.215 --> 09:54.510
Well, are you sure you're gonna be
all right here by yourself?

09:54.594 --> 09:56.053
I think so.

09:56.137 --> 09:59.015
[sighs] Okay.

09:59.098 --> 10:01.434
But if you need anything,
call Dad at work.

10:01.517 --> 10:03.394
- [softly] Okay.
- Okay.

10:03.477 --> 10:04.604
[kisses]

10:06.314 --> 10:07.356
Bye.

10:07.440 --> 10:08.941
Bye, sweetie.

10:14.572 --> 10:15.781
Lucas, do you copy?

10:17.033 --> 10:19.076
Lucas, come on, I know you're there!

10:19.160 --> 10:20.870
This is urgent.
I'm serious.

10:23.748 --> 10:26.292
I'm not gonna stop until you answer.

10:26.375 --> 10:27.793
Lucas.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.337
Lucas!

10:29.420 --> 10:31.213
Lucas, Lucas, Lucas,
Lucas, Lucas...

10:31.297 --> 10:33.591
Lucas, Lucas, Lucas, Lucas,
Lucas, Lucas, Lucas--

10:33.674 --> 10:35.134
Go away, Mike.

10:35.217 --> 10:38.220
I'm not in the mood, all right?
Over and out.

10:38.304 --> 10:39.680
No, not "out."

10:39.764 --> 10:42.224
I'm not messing around, okay?
This is about Will.

10:42.308 --> 10:44.226
- Over.
- What about Will?

10:45.227 --> 10:46.729
You mean about his funeral?
Over.

10:46.854 --> 10:47.980
No, not his funeral.

10:48.064 --> 10:49.565
- Screw his funeral!
- What?

10:49.649 --> 10:51.942
Just get over here stat.
And bring Dustin.

10:52.026 --> 10:53.319
Over and out.

10:56.530 --> 10:58.449
[sighs] What's taking so long?

10:59.367 --> 11:02.620
Well, everything's been a bit chaotic
around here without Gary.

11:03.412 --> 11:04.580
Without Gary?

11:05.581 --> 11:07.750
- Where's Gary?
- Well, I thought you knew.

11:07.833 --> 11:11.212
Those men from State, they...
they sent Gary home last night.

11:12.755 --> 11:14.673
So who did the autopsy?

11:15.257 --> 11:16.842
Someone from State.

11:38.072 --> 11:39.281
[coughs]

11:42.952 --> 11:45.830
He has a birth mark on his right arm.

11:45.913 --> 11:47.623
Can you show that to me, please?

11:53.087 --> 11:54.338
How's your mom doing?

11:57.758 --> 11:59.009
I don't know.

12:00.594 --> 12:03.472
How long's this stuff been going on?
With the lights and, uh...

12:03.556 --> 12:05.766
Will and the thing in the wall?

12:08.394 --> 12:10.729
Since the first phone call, I guess.

12:14.400 --> 12:17.403
You know, she's had anxiety problems...

12:17.486 --> 12:18.696
in the past.

12:20.281 --> 12:21.699
But this...

12:23.159 --> 12:24.410
I don't know.

12:24.493 --> 12:26.704
[breathes deeply]

12:29.123 --> 12:31.208
I'm worried it could be...

12:32.793 --> 12:34.211
Ugh, I don't know.

12:38.674 --> 12:40.092
She'll be okay.

12:41.177 --> 12:42.511
We'll be okay.

12:45.848 --> 12:47.266
My mom...

12:50.144 --> 12:51.979
she's tough. [chuckles]

12:52.104 --> 12:53.564
Yeah, she is.

12:56.108 --> 12:57.485
Hey.

12:59.028 --> 13:00.279
She is.

13:03.449 --> 13:04.492
[coroner] Ma'am!

13:04.575 --> 13:06.118
- Ma'am, I need you to sign!
- I don't...

13:06.202 --> 13:09.997
I don't know what you think that thing
is in there, but that is not my son!

13:10.080 --> 13:11.832
- Joyce, wait a second.
- No!

13:11.916 --> 13:14.043
- Mom!
- [coroner] Ma'am, I-- Ma'am!

13:16.545 --> 13:18.380
- [school bell ringing]
- [indistinct chatter]

13:18.464 --> 13:21.342
So, wait a sec. I don't understand.
You went back to my house?

13:21.425 --> 13:22.801
To look for Barb.

13:22.885 --> 13:24.970
Yeah, okay, but why didn't you
just talk to me?

13:25.054 --> 13:26.680
That's crazy.

13:26.764 --> 13:29.600
I don't know, I... I was scared.

13:29.683 --> 13:32.311
You seriously think
you saw a guy in a mask

13:32.394 --> 13:34.063
just hanging out in my yard?

13:34.146 --> 13:35.898
I don't think it was a mask.

13:35.981 --> 13:37.775
But he had no face?

13:38.943 --> 13:40.778
I don't know!

13:40.861 --> 13:42.738
I don't know, I just...

13:42.821 --> 13:45.407
I have a terrible feeling about this.

13:45.491 --> 13:46.534
Oh, this is bad.

13:46.617 --> 13:48.160
This is really bad.

13:48.244 --> 13:49.286
What?

13:50.204 --> 13:51.247
The cops...

13:52.164 --> 13:54.083
they're gonna want to talk
to all of us now.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.670
Tommy, Carol,
everybody who was at the party.

13:57.753 --> 13:59.713
- So?
- My parents are gonna murder me!

14:00.714 --> 14:02.758
Are you serious right now?

14:02.841 --> 14:04.927
You don't understand.
My dad's a grade-A asshole.

14:05.010 --> 14:08.514
Barb is missing!
And you're worried about your dad?

14:08.597 --> 14:11.934
Okay, just...
When you talk to the cops, just...

14:12.017 --> 14:13.936
don't mention the beers.

14:14.019 --> 14:15.813
It's just gonna get us both in trouble,

14:15.896 --> 14:18.023
and Barbara's got nothing to do with it,
okay?

14:18.107 --> 14:21.068
[scoffs] I can't believe you right now.

14:22.152 --> 14:24.154
- I can't believe you.
- Nancy.

14:25.781 --> 14:27.157
Nancy, wait!

14:28.617 --> 14:30.077
Nancy!

14:31.579 --> 14:33.038
- [Jonathan] Mom, will you get in?
- No, I...

14:33.122 --> 14:35.541
[stammers] I need to think.
Just go on home.

14:35.624 --> 14:37.585
Mom, will you just get in, please?

14:40.713 --> 14:41.881
Mom.

14:43.632 --> 14:44.717
Mom!

14:47.136 --> 14:48.178
Mom.

14:48.262 --> 14:50.639
- Stop.
- Just go home, Jonathan.

14:50.723 --> 14:53.475
No, this is not an okay time
for you to shut down.

14:53.559 --> 14:55.978
- Shut down? What...
- We have to deal with this, Mom.

14:56.061 --> 14:57.771
We have to deal with the funeral!

14:57.855 --> 14:59.315
The funeral?

14:59.398 --> 15:02.318
For... for who?
[loudly] For that thing back there?

15:02.401 --> 15:04.445
Okay, let me get this straight.

15:04.528 --> 15:07.698
Will, that's not his body,
because he's in the lights, right?

15:07.781 --> 15:09.617
And there's a monster in the wall?

15:09.700 --> 15:11.201
Do you even hear yourself?

15:12.161 --> 15:14.204
I know it sounds crazy.

15:14.288 --> 15:15.623
[stammers] I sound crazy!

15:15.706 --> 15:17.499
- Yeah.
- You think I don't know that?

15:17.583 --> 15:18.751
It is crazy!

15:18.834 --> 15:20.669
But I heard him, Jonathan.

15:20.753 --> 15:22.421
He talked to me!

15:22.504 --> 15:25.341
Will is... is calling to me!

15:25.424 --> 15:29.303
And he's out there, and he's alone,
and he's scared, and I...

15:29.386 --> 15:31.347
I don't care if anyone believes me!

15:31.430 --> 15:36.018
I am not gonna stop looking for him
until I find him and bring him home.

15:36.101 --> 15:39.188
[shouting] I am going to bring him home!

15:39.271 --> 15:42.066
[yelling] Yeah, well,
while you're talking to the lights,

15:42.149 --> 15:44.652
the rest of us are having
a funeral for Will!

15:44.735 --> 15:47.780
I'm not letting him sit in that freezer
another day!

15:48.405 --> 15:50.032
[Jonathan panting]

15:51.533 --> 15:53.202
All right, show's over.

15:55.204 --> 15:56.246
What?

16:04.296 --> 16:07.174
- [radio frequencies tuning]
- [indistinct whimpering]

16:09.593 --> 16:12.346
We keep losing the signal,
but you heard it, right?

16:12.429 --> 16:14.848
[Lucas] Yeah, I heard a baby.

16:14.932 --> 16:15.975
What?

16:16.058 --> 16:18.852
Mike, you obviously tapped
into a baby monitor.

16:18.978 --> 16:20.521
It's probably the Blackburns' next door.

16:20.604 --> 16:22.398
Uh, did that sound like a baby to you?

16:22.481 --> 16:23.774
- That was Will!
- Mike...

16:23.857 --> 16:26.068
Lucas, you don't understand.
He spoke last night.

16:26.151 --> 16:27.361
Words!

16:27.444 --> 16:30.197
He was singing that weird song he loves.
Even El heard him!

16:30.280 --> 16:32.491
Oh, well, if the weirdo heard him,
then I guess--

16:32.574 --> 16:33.826
Are you sure you're on the right channel?

16:33.909 --> 16:34.910
I don't think it's about that.

16:34.994 --> 16:38.664
I think, somehow, she's channeling him.

16:39.248 --> 16:41.417
- Like... like Professor X.
- Yeah.

16:41.500 --> 16:43.168
Are you actually believing this crap?

16:44.086 --> 16:45.129
I don't know, I mean...

16:45.212 --> 16:48.048
Do you remember when Will
fell off his bike and broke his finger?

16:48.132 --> 16:50.342
He sounded a lot like that.

16:51.010 --> 16:53.470
Did you guys not see what I saw?

16:53.554 --> 16:55.806
They pulled Will's body out of the water.

16:55.889 --> 16:57.433
He's dead!

16:59.768 --> 17:02.229
Well, maybe it's his ghost.
Maybe he's haunting us.

17:02.312 --> 17:03.981
- It's not his ghost.
- So how do you know that?

17:04.064 --> 17:05.733
- I just do!
- Then what was in that water?

17:05.816 --> 17:06.900
I don't know!

17:06.984 --> 17:09.194
All I know is Will is alive.

17:09.278 --> 17:10.738
Will is alive!

17:10.821 --> 17:12.156
He's out there somewhere.

17:12.239 --> 17:13.866
All we have to do is find him.

17:16.994 --> 17:18.704
[static crackling on radio]

17:20.456 --> 17:21.999
This isn't gonna work.

17:22.082 --> 17:23.959
We need to get El to a stronger radio.

17:24.710 --> 17:27.046
- Mr. Clarke's Heathkit ham shack.
- Yeah.

17:27.129 --> 17:28.172
The Heathkit's at school.

17:28.255 --> 17:32.509
There is no way we're gonna get the weirdo
in there without anyone noticing.

17:32.593 --> 17:35.471
I mean... look at her.

18:20.265 --> 18:21.558
Wow.

18:21.642 --> 18:23.685
- She looks--
- Pretty.

18:25.813 --> 18:27.106
Good.

18:27.189 --> 18:28.482
You look pretty good.

18:44.748 --> 18:45.999
[whispers] Pretty.

18:47.751 --> 18:48.961
Good.

19:33.505 --> 19:34.840
Clear.

19:38.510 --> 19:41.471
- You boys hear me all right in there?
- Loud and clear, Shepard.

19:42.389 --> 19:44.266
Good luck in there, son.

19:46.685 --> 19:48.645
[low growling]

20:17.341 --> 20:18.884
[monster growling]

20:44.701 --> 20:48.330
"The brown current ran swiftly
out of the heart of darkness,

20:48.413 --> 20:50.415
bearing us down towards the sea

20:50.499 --> 20:53.252
with twice the speed
of our upward progress.

20:54.169 --> 20:57.005
And Kurtz's life
was running swiftly, too--"

20:57.631 --> 20:59.549
Nancy Wheeler?

20:59.633 --> 21:01.510
If you'll come with me, please?

21:06.139 --> 21:09.935
[Powell] This argument
you and Barbara had?

21:10.018 --> 21:11.645
What exactly was it about?

21:13.522 --> 21:15.857
[Nancy] It wasn't really an argument.

21:16.775 --> 21:18.819
Barb just wanted to leave.

21:18.902 --> 21:21.029
I didn't, so, I...

21:22.823 --> 21:24.658
I told her to just go home.

21:25.659 --> 21:26.868
Then what?

21:27.995 --> 21:31.665
Then I went upstairs
to put on some dry clothes.

21:31.748 --> 21:34.626
And the next day, you went back and...

21:34.710 --> 21:36.128
saw a bear, you're thinking?

21:37.421 --> 21:40.841
I don't know what it was, but...

21:40.924 --> 21:42.134
I think...

21:43.260 --> 21:46.221
I think maybe it took Barb.

21:46.305 --> 21:48.598
- You need to check behind Steve's house--
- We did.

21:48.682 --> 21:50.017
There's nothing there.

21:50.100 --> 21:52.769
- There's no sign of a bear.
- And no car.

21:52.894 --> 21:54.021
- What?
- [Callahan] Look.

21:54.104 --> 21:56.356
We figure that Barbara
came back last night

21:56.440 --> 21:58.567
and then she took off,
went somewhere else.

21:58.650 --> 22:00.819
Has she ever talked to you
about running off?

22:00.902 --> 22:02.362
Leaving town, maybe?

22:02.446 --> 22:03.572
No.

22:03.655 --> 22:05.866
No, Barb wouldn't do that, ever.

22:05.949 --> 22:09.328
She wasn't maybe upset about the fact
that you were spending time with this boy?

22:09.411 --> 22:11.621
Uh, Steve Harrington?

22:11.705 --> 22:13.332
What? No!

22:13.415 --> 22:16.585
Maybe she was jealous
because she saw you go up to Steve's room?

22:16.668 --> 22:17.753
It wasn't like that.

22:17.836 --> 22:18.962
Like what?

22:19.046 --> 22:21.923
Steve and me, we're... we're just friends.

22:22.007 --> 22:23.759
We... we just talked.

22:23.842 --> 22:27.888
Now was this before or after
you changed out of your clothes?

22:32.434 --> 22:34.853
[Hopper] So, Gary, tell me
about these troopers that brought in Will.

22:34.936 --> 22:37.147
It was about six of 'em, I'd say.

22:37.230 --> 22:38.482
They're all Staties?

22:38.565 --> 22:39.566
Yes, sir.

22:39.649 --> 22:42.694
Never seen that many troopers
come with a body before.

22:42.778 --> 22:45.572
They told you that they were gonna
take care of the autopsy, huh?

22:45.655 --> 22:47.574
Yeah. Claimed jurisdiction.
Kicked me out.

22:47.657 --> 22:50.660
Well, it all seemed a bit over the top
to me, considering...

22:50.744 --> 22:52.579
Considering what?

22:52.662 --> 22:55.791
Considering this was Will Byers
and not John F. Kennedy.

22:57.042 --> 22:59.086
[indistinct chatter on TV]

23:01.129 --> 23:02.422
[sighs]

23:03.924 --> 23:06.426
- Thanks for stopping by, Gary.
- Sure thing.

23:06.510 --> 23:09.054
...let the people know that, uh,
the troopers are on duty

23:09.137 --> 23:12.682
and you should be safe, because we think
this is just an isolated incident.

23:12.766 --> 23:15.268
[reporter] State trooper David O'Bannon,
thank you so much for your help.

23:15.352 --> 23:16.937
[O'Bannon] Thank you, sir.
[reporter] Back to you...

23:38.250 --> 23:40.836
Okay, remember,
if anyone sees us, look sad.

23:40.919 --> 23:42.587
[man on PA] Attention students,

23:42.671 --> 23:47.342
there will be an assembly to honor
Will Byers in the gymnasium now.

23:47.425 --> 23:49.261
Do not go to fourth period.

23:49.344 --> 23:50.512
It's locked.

23:50.595 --> 23:52.764
- What?
- Hey, do you think you can open it?

23:52.848 --> 23:54.558
With your powers?

23:54.641 --> 23:56.101
Boys?

23:56.184 --> 23:57.185
[Lucas] Hey.

23:57.310 --> 23:58.770
Assembly's about to start.

23:58.854 --> 24:01.606
We know.
We're just, you know...

24:01.690 --> 24:03.483
Upset.

24:03.567 --> 24:04.860
[stammers] Yeah, definitely upset.

24:04.943 --> 24:06.403
We need some alone time.

24:06.486 --> 24:08.655
- To cry.
- [Mr. Clarke] Yeah, listen...

24:08.738 --> 24:09.990
I get it. I do.

24:10.073 --> 24:13.076
I know how hard this is,
but let's just be there for Will, huh?

24:13.577 --> 24:14.578
And then...

24:17.122 --> 24:19.583
the Heathkit is all yours
for the rest of the day.

24:19.666 --> 24:21.084
What do you say?

24:21.168 --> 24:23.670
[stammers] I don't believe we've met.
What's your name?

24:25.714 --> 24:27.424
- Eleven--
- Eleanor! She's my, uh--

24:27.507 --> 24:28.592
- Cousin.
- Second cousin.

24:28.675 --> 24:30.886
[Mike sighs]
She's here for Will's funeral.

24:30.969 --> 24:33.221
Ah, well, welcome to Hawkins Middle,
Eleanor.

24:33.305 --> 24:35.348
I wish you were here
under better circumstances.

24:35.432 --> 24:36.474
Thank you.

24:37.392 --> 24:39.144
Uh, where are you from exactly?

24:40.437 --> 24:41.605
Bad place--

24:41.688 --> 24:43.398
- Sweden!
- I have a lot of Swedish family.

24:43.481 --> 24:44.900
- [Dustin] She hates it there.
- Cold!

24:44.983 --> 24:47.569
Subzero.

24:49.029 --> 24:50.113
- Shall we?
- Yep!

24:51.448 --> 24:52.908
[principal] At times like these...

24:52.991 --> 24:56.828
it is important that we come together
as a community.

24:56.912 --> 24:59.122
- We come--
- [door bangs]

25:02.209 --> 25:03.627
Abort.

25:05.837 --> 25:08.215
We come together to heal...

25:09.424 --> 25:10.842
we come together to grieve...

25:12.344 --> 25:14.888
- You lied to the police!
- I didn't lie!

25:14.971 --> 25:17.224
[shouting] How naive do you think I am?

25:17.307 --> 25:19.434
You and Steve were just talking?

25:19.517 --> 25:20.769
[shouting] We slept together!

25:20.852 --> 25:23.104
Is that what you want to know?
It doesn't matter!

25:23.188 --> 25:26.524
- It does matter!
- No! It is all bullshit!

25:26.608 --> 25:28.818
It has nothing to do with Barb
and she's missing.

25:28.902 --> 25:30.779
And something terrible
happened to her. I know it.

25:30.862 --> 25:32.781
I know it!

25:32.864 --> 25:34.908
And no one is listening to me!

25:34.991 --> 25:36.534
Sweetie, sweetie, I'm listening.

25:36.618 --> 25:39.329
- I'm listening to you--
- No! You're not!

25:39.412 --> 25:41.414
Nancy... Nancy!

25:41.498 --> 25:43.208
Just leave me alone!

25:43.291 --> 25:44.542
[sighs]

25:51.508 --> 25:52.592
[crying]

26:17.867 --> 26:19.160
[gasps softly]

27:16.801 --> 27:18.219
[devices beeping]

27:19.346 --> 27:20.847
Try him again.

27:21.681 --> 27:23.558
Shepard, come in.
Confirm comm.

27:23.641 --> 27:25.143
[static crackling on radio]

27:25.226 --> 27:28.229
Shepard, come in.
Confirm comm.

27:28.938 --> 27:30.023
[static crackling]

27:30.106 --> 27:32.650
[Shepard on radio] This is Shepard.
Confirming, over.

27:33.651 --> 27:35.528
Shepard.
Where are you?

27:35.612 --> 27:39.032
Can you describe to us
what it is you see? Over.

27:39.115 --> 27:41.993
[Shepard] It's low visibility.
I'm about one click south of the rift.

27:42.077 --> 27:45.580
Everything's still here,
but it's all eroded. Covered in blood...

27:45.663 --> 27:46.956
[indistinct growling on radio]

27:47.040 --> 27:49.084
Shepard? Do you copy?

27:49.167 --> 27:51.002
[Shepard breathing heavily]

27:51.086 --> 27:53.338
Shepard?
Can you hear me?

27:53.421 --> 27:56.049
[Shepard] There's something else...
There's something else in here!

27:56.132 --> 27:57.592
[monster growling on radio]

27:57.675 --> 27:59.928
- [siren blaring]
- Reel him in.

28:00.011 --> 28:03.056
- [yelling] Reel him back in!
- [man] Get him in.

28:03.139 --> 28:04.516
Come on, come on!
Faster!

28:04.599 --> 28:06.101
[Shepard] There's something else in here!

28:06.184 --> 28:08.228
Pull me out!
Pull me out, pull me out!

28:08.311 --> 28:10.522
- Pull me out! Pull me out!
- [monster growling]

28:16.778 --> 28:18.571
[men shouting indistinctly]

28:31.167 --> 28:34.087
[man 1] Shepard, come in. Over.
[man 2] Comms are down, sir.

28:34.170 --> 28:35.755
[man 1] Shepard, come in!
Over.

29:00.321 --> 29:02.407
[monster growling]

29:06.161 --> 29:09.122
[principal] Will Byers' death
is an unimaginable tragedy.

29:09.956 --> 29:14.669
Will was an exceptional student
and a wonderful friend to all of us.

29:14.753 --> 29:20.258
It's impossible to express the hole
his loss will leave in our community.

29:21.301 --> 29:23.636
I'd like to introduce you to Sandy Sloane.

29:23.720 --> 29:26.389
She's a local grief counselor
from the church over in Jonesboro.

29:27.724 --> 29:29.100
But before she comes up here,

29:29.184 --> 29:33.354
I just want those of you who are having
trouble dealing with this tragic loss...

29:33.438 --> 29:34.606
Look at these fakers.

29:35.523 --> 29:37.442
They probably didn't even know
his name till today.

29:37.525 --> 29:39.152
- [Troy chuckling]
- [laughs] What?

29:39.235 --> 29:41.946
[Troy] Who is interested in this?
This is so stupid.

29:42.030 --> 29:44.491
- Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah...
- [chuckling]

29:44.574 --> 29:46.743
[Troy mocking] Oh,
he was such a great student.

29:46.826 --> 29:51.122
[mock crying] Oh, he's going to leave
a hole in the community.

29:51.206 --> 29:52.791
[Eleven] Mouth breather.

29:54.083 --> 29:56.294
[indistinct mocking continues]

30:01.674 --> 30:02.717
[school bell ringing]

30:04.803 --> 30:06.513
[indistinct chatter]

30:08.640 --> 30:10.975
Hey! Hey!

30:11.059 --> 30:12.310
Hey, Troy!

30:12.393 --> 30:13.561
Hey, Troy!

30:15.772 --> 30:17.607
You... you think this is funny?

30:17.690 --> 30:19.108
What'd you say, Wheeler?

30:19.192 --> 30:21.736
[stammers] I saw you guys
laughing over there.

30:21.820 --> 30:23.947
And I think that's
a real messed up thing to do.

30:24.030 --> 30:26.074
Didn't you listen to the counselor,
Wheeler?

30:26.157 --> 30:27.784
Grief shows itself in funny ways.

30:28.493 --> 30:31.871
[Troy] Besides, what's there to be
sad about, anyway?

30:31.955 --> 30:33.915
Will's in fairyland now, right?

30:33.998 --> 30:36.960
Flying around
with all the other little fairies.

30:37.043 --> 30:38.545
All happy and gay!

30:38.628 --> 30:40.839
[Troy imitating fairy]

30:48.888 --> 30:51.057
- [Troy grunts]
- [all exclaiming]

30:52.433 --> 30:54.143
[Troy] You're dead, Wheeler!

30:54.853 --> 30:55.937
Dead!

30:59.148 --> 31:00.900
[indistinct murmuring]

31:06.114 --> 31:08.658
[laughs] Dude, Troy peed himself.

31:08.741 --> 31:10.243
[all laughing]

31:12.912 --> 31:14.038
[giggles]

31:14.122 --> 31:15.874
[panting]

31:17.000 --> 31:18.501
[Dustin] Holy shit!

31:23.464 --> 31:25.091
Hey! What's going on here?

31:25.174 --> 31:26.259
Oh.

31:26.342 --> 31:28.428
Mike! Let's go!

31:36.477 --> 31:40.481
It's made of soft wood
with a crepe interior.

31:41.482 --> 31:44.986
Uh, now, I...
I don't know what your budget is,

31:45.069 --> 31:48.740
but over here, we...
we have copper and bronze.

31:50.116 --> 31:51.242
[Jonathan sighs]

31:55.455 --> 31:57.457
[stammers] Can you just give me a second?

31:57.540 --> 31:58.583
Of course.

32:03.588 --> 32:04.631
Hey.

32:05.381 --> 32:06.424
Hey.

32:07.717 --> 32:10.970
Your mom, um... she said you'd be here.

32:13.514 --> 32:14.599
I just...

32:14.682 --> 32:15.808
[inhales deeply]

32:17.185 --> 32:19.145
Can we talk for a second?

32:21.314 --> 32:24.400
[Jonathan] It looks like it could be
some kind of perspective distortion,

32:24.484 --> 32:26.527
but I wasn't using the wide angle.

32:28.112 --> 32:29.155
I don't know.

32:29.238 --> 32:30.448
It's weird.

32:33.493 --> 32:36.162
And you're sure you didn't see
anyone else out there?

32:36.245 --> 32:38.039
No.

32:38.122 --> 32:40.583
And she was there one second
and then, um...

32:41.668 --> 32:43.211
gone.

32:43.294 --> 32:44.921
I figured she bolted.

32:45.004 --> 32:47.340
The cops think that she ran away.

32:49.717 --> 32:51.344
But they don't know Barb.

32:51.427 --> 32:54.013
And I went back to Steve's...

32:55.223 --> 32:57.767
and I thought I...

32:57.850 --> 32:59.644
saw something.

32:59.727 --> 33:01.020
Some...

33:02.563 --> 33:04.273
weird man or...

33:05.650 --> 33:07.777
I don't know what it was.

33:12.490 --> 33:14.158
I'm sorry.

33:14.242 --> 33:18.162
I... I shouldn't have come
here today. I'm...

33:18.871 --> 33:20.081
I'm so sorry.

33:20.164 --> 33:21.541
What'd he look like?

33:24.210 --> 33:25.253
What?

33:25.336 --> 33:27.588
This man you saw in the woods.

33:28.381 --> 33:29.632
What'd he look like?

33:30.633 --> 33:33.636
[stammers] I don't know.

33:36.139 --> 33:38.433
It was almost like he...

33:38.516 --> 33:39.559
he didn't have--

33:39.642 --> 33:41.477
Didn't have a face?

33:43.479 --> 33:45.565
How did you know that?

33:56.284 --> 33:58.036
[indistinct chatter]

33:59.912 --> 34:01.247
Aw, come on!

34:03.082 --> 34:04.667
Another, please.

34:04.751 --> 34:06.711
And another for my, uh, friend here.

34:07.920 --> 34:09.756
Oh, thanks, man.
Appreciate it.

34:09.839 --> 34:12.425
Yeah, that's all right.
I'm, uh... I'm celebrating.

34:12.508 --> 34:15.386
My daughter,
she won the spelling bee today.

34:15.470 --> 34:16.637
[chuckling]

34:16.721 --> 34:17.722
Is that right?

34:17.805 --> 34:19.307
Yeah, that's right.

34:21.142 --> 34:22.685
"Odontalgia."

34:23.603 --> 34:24.645
That was the word.

34:24.729 --> 34:26.564
You know what it means?

34:26.647 --> 34:29.108
It's a fancy name for a toothache.

34:29.192 --> 34:30.234
[chuckles]

34:31.527 --> 34:35.073
Yeah, she's smart. She's real smart.
Don't know where she gets it from.

34:35.156 --> 34:37.450
I've been tryin'
to figure that out for years.

34:38.743 --> 34:40.244
Your daughter, she got a name?

34:44.082 --> 34:45.124
What?

34:45.208 --> 34:47.752
Your daughter?
What's her name?

34:49.420 --> 34:50.505
Sarah.

34:51.881 --> 34:53.007
Her name's Sarah.

34:55.468 --> 34:56.511
To Sarah.

35:06.813 --> 35:08.689
I recognize you.

35:08.773 --> 35:10.024
Are you famous or somethin'?

35:10.942 --> 35:14.403
Uh, you might have seen me on TV, I, uh...
I found that Byers boy.

35:16.864 --> 35:18.574
So, you on that case or what?

35:18.658 --> 35:20.326
I just saw him on patrol, you know?

35:20.409 --> 35:21.536
Dumb luck.

35:23.121 --> 35:25.414
So that quarry, that's, uh...

35:25.498 --> 35:27.917
that's state-run,
where they found the boy, huh?

35:29.293 --> 35:30.336
Yeah.

35:34.132 --> 35:36.717
[chuckling] Yeah, well, that's funny.

35:36.801 --> 35:40.054
'Cause, you know, I know for a fact
that it's run by the Sattler Company.

35:40.138 --> 35:43.975
Frank Sattler? Decent guy, still got
a couple operational quarries up in Roane.

35:44.058 --> 35:45.434
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

35:46.310 --> 35:47.562
That's right.

35:49.355 --> 35:50.815
So why are you lying to me, man?

35:54.026 --> 35:55.236
What's your problem, bud?

35:55.319 --> 35:56.946
I don't have a problem.

35:57.864 --> 35:59.490
I'm just a concerned citizen.

35:59.574 --> 36:00.741
Yeah?

36:00.825 --> 36:03.494
Well, stick your nose someplace else.

36:03.578 --> 36:04.871
The kid is dead.

36:04.954 --> 36:06.122
End of story.

36:09.000 --> 36:11.085
Thanks for ruining the game, dick.

36:15.673 --> 36:17.300
[grunting]

36:19.552 --> 36:20.636
[Hopper panting] Okay...

36:20.720 --> 36:22.680
- Let's try this one more time.
- [groaning]

36:22.763 --> 36:24.765
Who told you to be out there?

36:24.849 --> 36:26.601
What were you doing out there?

36:27.685 --> 36:30.104
I don't know!
I don't know. They...

36:30.229 --> 36:34.442
they just told me to call it in
and not let anybody get too close.

36:34.525 --> 36:36.152
Get close to what?

36:36.235 --> 36:37.486
The body.

36:39.113 --> 36:40.156
Who do you work for?

36:40.239 --> 36:42.700
The NSA? Hawkins Lab?

36:43.659 --> 36:45.620
- Who is that?
- [engine starts]

36:45.703 --> 36:47.580
- You're gonna get us both killed.
- Who is that?

36:47.663 --> 36:50.082
Hey! Hey!

36:50.166 --> 36:52.043
[tires screeching]

36:53.544 --> 36:55.254
[panting]

37:06.140 --> 37:08.059
["Should I Stay or Should I Go" playing]

37:09.018 --> 37:11.687
Come on!
Come on!

37:13.814 --> 37:15.524
Talk to me!

37:15.608 --> 37:17.902
I know you're here!

37:21.614 --> 37:22.782
[Mike] Come on.

37:27.245 --> 37:29.789
- Now what?
- She'll find him.

37:29.872 --> 37:30.998
Right, El?

37:31.082 --> 37:33.042
[radio frequencies tuning]

37:41.550 --> 37:42.718
[water pouring]

37:42.802 --> 37:44.136
Eleven?

37:46.222 --> 37:47.765
Are you listening?

37:50.559 --> 37:52.645
That man before you...

37:56.482 --> 37:58.401
I need you to find him.

38:03.656 --> 38:06.158
- [Eleven softly] Hurt him?
- No.

38:06.242 --> 38:08.828
No, I don't want you to hurt him.

38:10.413 --> 38:12.456
I want you to listen to him.

38:16.210 --> 38:17.837
- Listen?
- Yes.

38:18.838 --> 38:23.342
I want you to listen to what he says
and repeat his words back to me.

38:24.677 --> 38:27.930
Just like we used to
with those old nursery rhymes.

38:28.014 --> 38:29.432
Do you remember?

38:30.683 --> 38:32.184
Hmm?

38:32.310 --> 38:34.395
Do you think you can do that for me?

38:36.355 --> 38:38.149
- Mmm-hmm.
- Good.

38:56.000 --> 38:57.084
[man 1 on PA] Begin.

38:58.002 --> 38:59.003
[man 2] Amulet.

38:59.920 --> 39:00.921
Frigid.

39:01.756 --> 39:02.882
Evolve.

39:04.008 --> 39:05.051
Airplane.

39:06.052 --> 39:07.303
Eleven?

39:08.429 --> 39:10.056
Repeat the words.

39:15.102 --> 39:16.812
[man 2 on PA] Apricot.

39:16.937 --> 39:18.981
Peninsula.

39:19.065 --> 39:20.816
Game.

39:20.900 --> 39:22.360
Enchantment.

39:23.277 --> 39:24.445
Mouse.

39:25.613 --> 39:26.781
Balloon.

39:27.490 --> 39:28.616
She's doing it.

39:28.699 --> 39:30.409
- She's finding him!
- This is crazy.

39:30.493 --> 39:32.286
Calm down.
She just closed her eyes.

39:32.370 --> 39:33.496
[boys gasp]

39:33.579 --> 39:35.706
- Holy...
- [clanging]

39:39.877 --> 39:41.545
[clanging intensifies]

39:43.589 --> 39:44.840
What is that?

39:46.092 --> 39:47.802
- [radio tuning]
- [clanging continues]

39:47.885 --> 39:49.887
["Should I Stay or Should I Go" playing]

39:49.970 --> 39:51.013
[clanging]

39:52.515 --> 39:53.766
[clanging]

39:55.226 --> 39:57.311
- [music stops]
- [clanging]

39:59.730 --> 40:01.732
[child whimpering]

40:02.733 --> 40:03.776
[voice echoes] Mom?

40:03.859 --> 40:05.778
[gasps] Will?

40:05.861 --> 40:07.279
[Will on radio] Mom?

40:08.364 --> 40:09.657
No way!

40:10.324 --> 40:11.534
- [Will] Mom...
- Will!

40:11.617 --> 40:12.660
[Will] Please...

40:12.743 --> 40:14.078
Will!

40:14.912 --> 40:16.080
Will!

40:18.165 --> 40:19.208
Will...

40:20.626 --> 40:21.669
Will!

40:21.752 --> 40:23.087
- [Will] Mom!
- Will!

40:23.170 --> 40:25.589
I'm here! I'm here!

40:25.673 --> 40:26.882
- Oh, God...
- [echoing] Mom!

40:26.966 --> 40:28.926
- Will!
- Will, it's us! Are you there?

40:29.009 --> 40:30.386
Can you hear us?
We're here!

40:30.469 --> 40:32.471
[Will distorted] Hello? Mom?

40:32.555 --> 40:33.597
Why can't he hear us?

40:33.681 --> 40:34.890
I don't know!

40:36.600 --> 40:37.768
Baby...

40:37.852 --> 40:40.646
- Mom?
- Oh, God. Will!

40:40.729 --> 40:41.730
[echoing] Mom!

40:42.356 --> 40:43.774
[Joyce] Oh, thank God.

40:43.858 --> 40:45.651
[crying] Baby...

40:45.734 --> 40:46.777
Will...

40:46.861 --> 40:48.988
- [monster growling]
- Mom...

40:49.071 --> 40:50.406
Mom, it's coming!

40:50.489 --> 40:52.700
Tell me where you are!
How do I get to you?

40:52.783 --> 40:55.286
[echoing] It's like home,
but it's so dark...

40:55.369 --> 40:59.248
It's so dark and empty.
And it's cold!

40:59.331 --> 41:00.541
Mom? Mom!

41:00.624 --> 41:03.919
Listen to me!
I swear I'm gonna get to you, okay?

41:04.003 --> 41:05.838
But right now, I need you to hide.

41:05.921 --> 41:07.298
Mom, please!

41:07.381 --> 41:09.967
- No, no, listen! Listen, I...
- [growling continues]

41:10.050 --> 41:13.012
I will find you, but you have to run now!

41:13.095 --> 41:15.431
- Run! Run!
- [monster screeching]

41:17.266 --> 41:18.767
- [fuse blowing]
- [boys yelp]

41:20.060 --> 41:22.855
- [boys exclaiming]
- [fire alarm ringing]

41:26.942 --> 41:28.068
[alarm continues]

41:33.699 --> 41:34.992
[yells]

41:40.039 --> 41:41.290
[alarm ringing]

41:41.373 --> 41:42.583
- El, are you okay?
- [Lucas] Oh!

41:44.627 --> 41:45.711
Can you move?

41:48.881 --> 41:50.132
Here, help her up.

41:54.136 --> 41:55.221
[grunting]

42:07.525 --> 42:09.318
[birds chirping]

42:09.401 --> 42:10.903
[sobs softly]

42:24.083 --> 42:26.293
- [alarm ringing]
- [Mike] This way!

42:32.841 --> 42:34.260
[Nancy] And you're...

42:34.343 --> 42:36.679
[Jonathan] Brightening.
Enlarging.

42:36.762 --> 42:37.888
[Nancy] Hmm.

42:40.766 --> 42:43.018
- Did your mom say anything else?
- [grunts]

42:43.102 --> 42:47.147
Like, um,
where it might have gone to, or...

42:47.231 --> 42:50.651
- No, just that it came out of the wall.
- [machine dings]

42:52.236 --> 42:53.696
[Jonathan sighs]

42:57.825 --> 42:59.034
[Nancy] How long does this take?

42:59.994 --> 43:01.203
Not long.

43:03.622 --> 43:06.083
Have you been...

43:06.166 --> 43:08.002
doing this a while?

43:08.085 --> 43:09.670
What?

43:09.753 --> 43:11.005
Photography?

43:12.673 --> 43:13.716
Yeah.

43:14.633 --> 43:18.804
I guess I'd rather observe
people than, you know...

43:19.722 --> 43:20.931
Talk to them.

43:21.015 --> 43:22.975
I know.
It's weird.

43:23.058 --> 43:24.059
No!

43:24.184 --> 43:26.270
[stammers] No, it is.

43:26.353 --> 43:27.855
It's just, sometimes...

43:28.856 --> 43:31.567
people don't really say
what they're really thinking.

43:32.484 --> 43:34.403
But you capture the right moment...

43:35.321 --> 43:36.655
it says more.

43:36.739 --> 43:38.115
What was I saying?

43:39.033 --> 43:40.743
What?

43:40.826 --> 43:42.119
When you took my picture.

43:43.871 --> 43:45.456
I shouldn't have taken that.

43:47.541 --> 43:48.667
I'm, uh...

43:48.751 --> 43:50.294
I'm sorry.

43:52.212 --> 43:53.672
It's just--

43:53.756 --> 43:55.299
That's it.

43:56.717 --> 43:58.344
That's what I saw.

44:00.054 --> 44:01.138
[Jonathan gasps]

44:01.221 --> 44:02.806
My mom...

44:02.890 --> 44:04.850
I thought she was crazy

44:04.933 --> 44:06.685
'cause she said...

44:06.769 --> 44:09.521
that's not Will's body.
That he's alive.

44:09.605 --> 44:12.274
- And if he's alive--
- Then Barbara.

44:31.335 --> 44:33.337
- Hey, Patty!
- Hey, uh, need something, Chief?

44:33.420 --> 44:35.923
- Oh, you know, I forgot my hat.
- Oh.

44:36.006 --> 44:37.716
[laughing] I'll just be a minute.

44:42.012 --> 44:45.891
Hey, I love that book.
It's a nasty mutt.

44:45.974 --> 44:47.017
Hey, you can't be back here.

44:47.101 --> 44:48.686
Yeah, I just got off the line
with O'Bannon.

44:48.769 --> 44:50.729
He said that he needs
to see you at the station.

44:50.813 --> 44:52.898
- It's some emergency...
- What the hell are you talking about?

44:52.981 --> 44:54.108
I don't work with O'Bannon.

44:54.191 --> 44:55.984
Did I say O'Bannon? I meant...

44:58.278 --> 44:59.988
[smacks lips] Okay.

45:00.072 --> 45:01.407
[both grunt]

45:02.658 --> 45:04.034
[panting]

46:00.674 --> 46:01.842
[gasps]

46:10.100 --> 46:11.268
[exhales heavily]

46:24.573 --> 46:26.074
[breathing heavily]

47:00.234 --> 47:01.860
[car approaching]

47:14.206 --> 47:15.249
[groans]

47:22.339 --> 47:23.799
Babe...

47:23.882 --> 47:25.217
Jesus, the hell happened?

47:25.300 --> 47:26.510
[Joyce sobbing]

47:27.761 --> 47:28.929
Lonnie.

48:06.592 --> 48:08.594
[theme music playing]
